<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Fitzgerald called the clinic and was seen the same day. Two days ago she began vomiting, and since then she has had watery diarrhea six or seven times a day; her roommate had the same illness last week and recovered in two days. She has kept down only sips of water and tea. She has taken lithium 300 mg twice daily throughout, including last night&apos;s dose about 13 hours ago, because she was afraid of becoming ill again if she missed it. Since yesterday her hands shake more than usual and she feels queasy and washed out. She has had no confusion, slurred speech, unsteadiness, or muscle jerks, no blood in the stool, and no severe abdominal pain. She has not taken any painkillers. She took risperidone last night. Her mood has been steady and she has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Two days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Abdomen; generalized</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Two days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Vomiting, then watery diarrhea six or seven times a day</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Keeping down only sips of fluid</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Diarrhea through the day and night; vomiting easing today</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Roommate had the same illness last week; lithium started two weeks ago and taken throughout</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>No medicine taken for it</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Worse fine tremor, nausea, tiredness, feeling warm; no confusion, slurred speech, unsteadiness, blood in the stool, or thoughts of suicide or self-harm</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

