<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral gastroenteritis with mild dehydration (A08.4)</content>. Probable viral gastroenteritis, like her roommate&apos;s illness, with mild dehydration: dry mouth, a faster pulse, lower blood pressure, a creatinine of 1.08 mg/dL from 0.72, sodium 134 and potassium 3.4 mmol/L. No blood in the stool and no severe pain, so no stool tests or antibiotics are needed. [S]<list><item>Oral rehydration solution in small, frequent sips, then normal food as tolerated.</item><item>No anti-diarrheal or anti-inflammatory medicines.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lithium level above the therapeutic range with dehydration (T43.595A)</content>. Lithium 1.4 mmol/L, about 13 hours after the last dose, from dehydration and a lower kidney filtration while she kept taking it. The worse tremor and nausea fit a mildly raised level; there is no confusion, unsteadiness, or myoclonus, so she can be managed at home with fluids while lithium is held. [S]<list><item>Hold lithium for 48 hours, then restart at the same dose once she is eating and drinking normally.</item><item>Care coordinator phone check tomorrow.</item><item>Go to the emergency department for confusion, unsteadiness, slurred speech, a coarse tremor, or if she cannot keep fluids down.</item><item>Lithium level, kidney function, and electrolytes at the visit in one week.</item><item>A written lithium sick-day plan.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">First episode of psychosis with marked mood symptoms, provisional diagnosis (F29)</content>. No manic or psychotic symptoms. Missing two days of lithium carries little risk of relapse; this was explained, because she was afraid to stop it. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline are in her phone. [S]<list><item>Continue risperidone 2 mg at bedtime.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Canadian Network for Mood and Anxiety Treatments (CANMAT) and International Society for Bipolar Disorders (ISBD) 2018 guidelines for the management of patients with bipolar disorder (2018); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); 2017 Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Management of Infectious Diarrhea (2017)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Phone check tomorrow. Visit in one week with lithium level, kidney function, and electrolytes, or sooner as above. Next scheduled visit 1930-06-08: lithium level after the sick visit, prolactin, and the antipsychotic plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

